  "goodToKnow": "Der Bergbau is mining. The Ruhrgebiet and the Saarland were built on coal mining, and in December 2018 Germany's last hard-coal mine, Prosper-Haniel in Bottrop, closed. Lignite (Braunkohle) is still mined in open pits until the planned coal exit. A miner is der Bergmann (plural: Bergleute), a mine das Bergwerk, and the miners' greeting Glück auf! is still heard in the Ruhr. It has no plural."
